<title>BRAZIL: Ships loading/unloading commodities, Brazil ports.</title>
<headline>Ships loading/unloading commodities, Brazil ports.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following ships were loading, unloading, despatched or announced at the Brazilian ports of Paranagua and Antonina on Sept 12, port authorities reported. Quantities are in tonnes.</p>
<p>Berthed								 Agent</p>
<p>Barcaca A. Fatima unldg	 26,760   wheat		Orion</p>
<p>Flag Leader	 ldg	   31,793   soypellets	 Tibagi</p>
<p>Kapitan Banglay   ldg	    7,000   bag sugar	  Marcon</p>
<p>Nadelhorn	   ldg	   25,000   sugar	    Williams</p>
<p>Solon		 ldg	   14,000   bag sugar	Estinave</p>
<p>Sapanca	     ldg	   19,000   sugar	     Cargill</p>
<p>Powst.Listopadowy ldg	   29,500   soypellets	Cargill</p>
<p>Aghias Trias	ldg	   76,000   soybean/pellet  Cargill</p>
<p>Waiting to Berth</p>
<p>Hua Ting	    to load     12,000   bag sugar	 Orion</p>
<p>Expected</p>
<p>Princefield	 to unload    3,006   barley</p>
<p>Marcon Theogennitor to load    66,250  soybean/pellet</p>
<p>Marcon	     despatched</p>
<p>--Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
